599
00:26:45.430 --> 00:26:47.850
He's the best human being ever.

600
00:26:47.850 --> 00:26:55.810
And I think at the time he was like six or seven, we played horse in his front yard.

601
00:26:56.190 --> 00:26:59.850
Like every day after school, he would like, come on, we got to play horse.

602
00:27:00.030 --> 00:27:00.250
And I'm like, okay.

603
00:27:00.250 --> 00:27:01.390
So you were shooting hoops.

604
00:27:02.030 --> 00:27:05.250
That was the extent of it, and I was terrible at it.

605
00:27:05.350 --> 00:27:06.930
I was absolutely terrible at it.

606
00:27:06.990 --> 00:27:11.250
But my dad and my brother had taught me how to play basketball when I was a kid.

607
00:27:11.310 --> 00:27:15.650
But all I ever did was play horse, and I think my dad, at the most, would pick me up

608
00:27:15.650 --> 00:27:17.390
and help me shoot the basket.

609
00:27:17.390 --> 00:27:18.810
I was horrible at basketball.

610
00:27:18.990 --> 00:27:20.130
I couldn't dribble or anything.

611
00:27:20.130 --> 00:27:22.370
So what did you say to Marla when she asked you?

612
